  "prefLabel": "Dec 201.03 Practice Before the Committee",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 201.03 Practice Before the Committee.\n\n(a) Any person may appear before the committee:\n\n(1) On one’s own behalf;\n\n(2) By an attorney authorized to practice in any state or the District of Columbia and in good standing; or\n\n(3) By an employee or authorized agent.\n\n(b) Any person appearing before the committee shall adhere to:\n\n(1) These rules; and\n\n(2) Any orders of the committee or agreements among parties including orders or agreements concerning confidentiality.\n\n(c) Nothing in these rules shall be interpreted in such a way as to permit the unauthorized practice of law, nor shall this rule in any way be construed to restrict or limit the right of any person to conduct his or her own representation with or before the committee.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A, eff 4-24-08",
